<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Communicate</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>say &lt;words&gt;                  ' &lt;words&gt; for short
ask &lt;character&gt; &lt;question&gt;
whisper &lt;character&gt; &lt;words&gt;
tell &lt;character&gt; &lt;words&gt;
shout &lt;words&gt;
comm add &lt;channel&gt;           then &lt;channel&gt; &lt;words&gt;
</pre>
<p>There are many ways to talk with other players:
</p>
<ul><li><b>say</b> speaks to everyone in the room. ' is short for say, so mind the space: a mistyped ' can turn into some other command.</li>
<li><b>ask</b> asks someone in the room a question; the others in the room hear it too.</li>
<li><b>whisper</b> speaks to one person in the room; the others see that you whisper, but not what.</li>
<li><b>tell</b> reaches one player anywhere in the world; nobody else hears it. A player can turn off tells (see <a cmd='#'>Help Tell</a>).</li>
<li><b>shout</b> reaches everyone in the game who isn't asleep or has turned shouts off. You must be level 5 to shout, and it costs endurance. Shout sparingly: most players find it annoying. Swearing in a shout takes your voice away for an hour.</li>
<li><b>channels</b> are the best place for chatter: newbie, chat and others, and any you start yourself (see <a cmd='#'>Help Comm</a>).</li></ul>
<p>To act out what your character does, see <a cmd='#'>Help Emotes</a> and <a cmd='#'>Help Socials</a>; 
to write to someone who isn't in the game, see <a cmd='#'>Help Mail</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
